  <section num="42 U.S.C. § 12182" title="Prohibition of discrimination by public accommodations" source="USCODE-2024-title42-chap126-subchapIII-sec12182.htm">
    <paragraph lga:provision="US-ADA-12182-a" lga:citation="42 U.S.C. § 12182(a)"
               lga:url="https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/42/12182"
               lga:regulates="Accessibility">No individual shall be discriminated against on the basis of disability in the full and equal enjoyment of the goods, services, facilities, privileges, advantages, or accommodations of any place of public accommodation by any person who owns, leases (or leases to), or operates a place of public accommodation.</paragraph>
  </section>
